## Step 1 — Deploy the Backend on EC2

### 1.1 Launch an EC2 Instance

1. Go to **AWS Console → EC2 → Launch Instance**
2. AMI: **Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS** (free tier eligible)
3. Instance type: **t3.micro** (free tier)
4. Key pair: Create new → download `.pem` file, keep it safe
5. **Network settings → Edit → Add rules:**
   - SSH port 22 (from your IP)
   - Custom TCP port **2000** from Anywhere — backend API
   - Custom UDP ports **10000–60000** from Anywhere — WebRTC media
6. Storage: 20 GB gp3
7. Click **Launch Instance**

### 1.2 SSH Into Your Instance

```bash
chmod 400 your-key.pem
ssh -i your-key.pem ubuntu@<YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP>
```

### 1.3 Install Node.js + PM2

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Node.js 20 LTS
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt install -y nodejs git

node -v    # v20.x
npm -v

# PM2 — keeps your server alive and restarts on reboot
sudo npm install -g pm2
```

### 1.4 Clone Your Repo and Install Dependencies

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/ai-interviewer.git
cd ai-interviewer/backend
npm install
```

### 1.5 Add Your .env File

```bash
nano .env
```

```
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=your_deepgram_key
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
JWT_SECRET=your_secret
```

### 1.6 Run Database Migrations

```bash
npx prisma migrate deploy
```

### 1.7 Start With PM2

```bash
pm2 start "npx tsx src/index.ts" --name ai-interviewer-backend
pm2 save
pm2 startup    # copy-paste the command it gives you

pm2 status     # should show "online"
pm2 logs ai-interviewer-backend
```

Backend is now live at: `http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:2000`

