## Step 3 — HTTPS for the Backend (Required for Production)

Browsers also require the WebRTC signaling endpoint to be HTTPS. Set up Nginx + Let's Encrypt.

### On EC2:

```bash
sudo apt install -y nginx certbot python3-certbot-nginx
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/ai-interviewer
```

Paste:
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name your-domain.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:2000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}
```

```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/ai-interviewer /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl restart nginx

# Get free SSL cert (requires a domain name)
sudo certbot --nginx -d your-domain.com
```

> [!TIP]
> **Free domains:** Use [duckdns.org](https://duckdns.org) or [freenom.com](https://freenom.com) to get a free subdomain pointing to your EC2 IP, then get a free SSL cert with Certbot.

